The OWASP category list in report_service.py is still the 2023 edition —
Insecure Output Handling, Training Data Poisoning, Model Denial of Service,
Insecure Plugin Design, Overreliance and Model Theft were all superseded by
the 2025 list and again by the 2026 edition published on 2026-08-03. Reports
generated today therefore map findings to categories that no longer exist.

Updates the canonical list to the 2026 edition:

  2023                              2026
  LLM01 Prompt Injection         -> LLM01 Prompt Injection
  LLM02 Insecure Output Handling -> LLM10 Improper Output Handling
  LLM03 Training Data Poisoning  -> LLM05 Data and Model Poisoning
  LLM04 Model Denial of Service  -> LLM06 Unbounded Consumption
  LLM05 Supply-Chain Vulns       -> LLM04 Supply Chain
  LLM06 Sensitive Info Disclosure-> LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure
  LLM07 Insecure Plugin Design   -> folded into LLM01 / LLM03
  LLM08 Excessive Agency         -> LLM03 Excessive Agency
  LLM09 Overreliance             -> LLM07 Misinformation
  LLM10 Model Theft              -> no longer an OWASP category

New in the current list and now represented: LLM08 Hidden Context Exposure
and LLM09 Vector and Embedding Weaknesses.

Changes:
- backend/app/services/report_service.py: OWASP_LLM_TOP10 replaced with the
  2026 entries, each lab association carried across to the renumbered risk.
- frontend threat-models/page.tsx: per-lab codes remapped to match.
- README: per-lab OWASP column, the coverage table, and the coverage total.
  Coverage reads 7 of 10 rather than 8 of 10, because Model Theft is gone as
  a category while Misinformation and Hidden Context Exposure are now listed
  with no dedicated lab. The RAG Poisoning lab picks up LLM09, which had no
  2023 equivalent.

Two judgment calls worth your review, since they are about lab content
rather than the standard:
- Memory Poisoning now maps to LLM05 Data and Model Poisoning (it previously
  sat under Excessive Agency and Sensitive Information Disclosure in the
  frontend map, which looked like a poor fit).
- RAG Poisoning picks up LLM09 Vector and Embedding Weaknesses alongside
  LLM05. Happy to adjust either if your labs behave differently than their
  names suggest.

Also fixes a pre-existing inconsistency: the frontend mapped
autonomous_agent to the old LLM04 (Model Denial of Service) while the
backend list had no labs under it. It is now LLM03 only, matching both the
backend list and the README.

MITRE ATLAS technique mappings are unchanged. Challenge content, flags and
lab behaviour are untouched — this is a labelling change only.

Verified: report_service imports and the list parses to 10 entries in
LLM01..LLM10 order; frontend codes reference only categories the backend
list marks as covered.

Signed-off-by: Animesh Shaw <animeshshaw@pm.me>
